            0.15,
            0.087,
            0.665,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Calculating using estimation and approximation —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.112,
            0.847,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Describe the relationships among the quantities that are needed to find the answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.149,
            0.846,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Make reasonable assumptions and approximations if the required information is not available."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.186,
            0.847,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Compute and find the answer (and check how close your guess was)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.226,
            0.848,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Would the number of coins be in hundreds, thousands, lakhs, crores, or even more? Make an instinctive guess."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.273,
            0.65,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find the answer by making necessary and reasonable assumptions and approximations for the unknowns. Remember, we are not looking for an exact answer but a reasonably close estimate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.669,
            0.288,
            0.875,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How about measuring to find out the weight of a 1-rupee coin?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.378,
            0.187,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.102,
                0.378,
                0.187,
                0.434
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.373,
            0.825,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Initially, your guesses may be very far off from the answer and it is perfectly fine! You will get better at it like as you do it often and in different situations. Guessing and estimating can build intuition about numbers and various quantities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.463,
            0.846,
            0.501
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Estu asks, “What if we use 5-rupee coins or 10-rupee notes instead? How much money could it be?”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.503,
            0.847,
            0.561
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Make an instinctive guess first. Then find out (make necessary and reasonable assumptions about the unknown details and find the answers)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.565,
            0.847,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Estu says, “When I become an adult, I would like to donate notebooks worth my weight every year”. Roxie says, “When I grow up, I would like to do annadāna (offering grains or meals) worth my weight every year”."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.632,
            0.802,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ How many people might benefit from each of these offerings in a year? Again, guess first before finding out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.619,
            0.903,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.818,
                0.619,
                0.903,
                0.67
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.675,
            0.848,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Roxie and Estu overheard someone saying—“We did pādayātra for about 400 km to reach this place! We arrived early this morning.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.723,
            0.673,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ How long ago would they have started their journey?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.759,
            0.846,
            0.8
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Find answers by making necessary assumptions and approximations. Do guess first before calculating to check how close your guess was!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.822,
            0.837,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note to the Teacher:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Assumptions can vary greatly at times, and as a result the answers computed using these you can also vary. This is perfectly alright. Modelling the situation properly is crucial, which can also be done in different ways sometimes. The accuracy of the assumed numbers or quantities can get better with exposure and practice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
